[0.013, "o", "\u001b[?1049h\u001b[22;0;0t\u001b[1;30r\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4l\u001b[?7h\u001b[?1h\u001b="]
[0.002, "o", "\u001b[39;49m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[26d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[J\u001b[5d"]
[0.000, "o", "As the sun sets on the plains, Sheriff Cheney angrily snaps on the cuffs. You are shoved into the\r\u001b[6d"]
[0.000, "o", "coach and land on top of Muddy Charlie and a pile of silver dollars, which until recently had been\r\u001b[7d"]
[0.000, "o", "the property of the Missouri, Kansas & Texas Line.\r\u001b[9d"]
[0.000, "o", "Muddy whispers, \"Don't fret none, Rick! You done good blowing up that tunnel -- I just didn't plan\r\u001b[10d"]
[0.000, "o", "on the sheriff getting word ahead of time, is all. That were powerful bad luck.\"\r\u001b[12dThe sheriff climbs onto his horse, spits, and you begin to rumble forward. \"You boys really got it\r\u001b[13d"]
[0.000, "o", "coming this time,\" he yells back cheerfully.\r\u001b[15d"]
[0.000, "o", "Muddy shakes his head. \"No offense, Sheriff, but I reckon you got the wrong men. We was just on our\r\u001b[16d"]
[0.000, "o", "way to the theater.\"\r\u001b[18d"]
[0.000, "o", "The sheriff disagrees. \"The only place you boys are heading is straight to the...\r\u001b[20d\u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mHoosegow\r\u001b[21d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mA Wild West Wreck by Ben Collins-Sussman and Jack Welch\r\u001b[22d"]
[0.000, "o", "Release 16 / Serial number 130320 / Inform 7 build 6G60 (I6/v6.32 lib 6/12N)\r\u001b[23dType \"help\" for instructions and \"hints\" for hints -- or just roll into town guns a-blazin'.\r\u001b[25d[Press Space To Continue]\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[2.504, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[37m\u001b[40mIn the twilight, you sight the sheriff's sturdy brick office near the edge of town. \"That's mighty\r\u001b[2d"]
[0.000, "o", "fine construction,\" notes Muddy, sounding less feisty now. \"Mighty fine indeed.\" The coach rolls to\r\u001b[3d"]
[0.000, "o", "a halt and a thick arm yanks you roughly from your seat. You land awkwardly in the rutted street,\r\u001b[4d"]
[0.000, "o", "where the sheriff holds you in place with the heel of one boot. He yells to his men, \"Bring the\r\u001b[5d"]
[0.000, "o", "coach around back, we got to \u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[3m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mimpound\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[23m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m that evidence.\" You are shoved into the sheriff's office and\r\u001b[6d"]
[0.000, "o", "then into a small holding cell.\u001b[K\r\u001b[7d\u001b[K\u001b[8d"]
[0.000, "o", "The deputy wakes with a start, whips his dusty boots off the desk and stands, tucking his shirt back\u001b[9;1Hinto his pants. The sheriff gives him a brief, judgmental glance and offhandedly tosses an arrest\u001b[K\r\u001b[10dwarrant on the desk. He barks, \"Jimbo, listen up. Picked up these two down near the train. A federal\u001b[11;1H"]
[0.000, "o", "marshal will be coming for them at eight o'clock tomorrow morning. There's going to be a hanging!\"\u001b[12;5H"]
[0.000, "o", "deputy nods slowly. The sheriff continues, \"Please take care of our 'guests'. I got to head down\u001b[13;1H"]
[0.000, "o", "to Wichita Falls to discuss my invention with some \u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[3m\u001b[37m\u001b[40minvestors\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[23m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m, so you is in charge.\" The deputy\r\u001b[14dsmiles until the sheriff adds, \"Jimbo, don't screw up,\" as he heads out the door.\r\u001b[15d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[K\u001b[16d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mJail Cell\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[K\r\u001b[17d"]
[0.000, "o", "Why are you not surprised to have landed right back in the hoosegow after another one of Muddy's\r\u001b[18d"]
[0.000, "o", "dubious plans? Will you ever learn? How did it come to this?\u001b[K\r\u001b[20d"]
[0.000, "o", "The small jail cell is brick on three sides, metal bars on the other, with a tightly locked gate. A\r\u001b[21d"]
[0.000, "o", "small window is set into the brickwork above your head. Through the jail bars you can see the\r\u001b[22dsheriff's office.\u001b[K\r\u001b[23d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[K\u001b[24d"]
[0.000, "o", "A broken stool lies on the floor.\r\u001b[25d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[K\u001b[26d"]
[0.000, "o", "Muddy leans against the wall tapping a harmonica on his arm.\r\u001b[28dIn the corner of the cell, a disheveled man in a black suit is stretched out on a crude wooden bench\u001b[29;1H"]
[0.000, "o", "and is snoring loudly, oblivious to your presence.\r\u001b[30d[MORE]"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[2.506, "o", "\r"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[5S\u001b[H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m Jail Cell                                                                          Score: 0/24     \u001b[25;1H\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[K\u001b[26d"]
[0.000, "o", "A dented food bowl sits on the office floor, only a few feet from the jail bars.\r\u001b[28d"]
[0.000, "o", "In the office you can also see the deputy.\r\u001b[30d>\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
